+# Custom Scripts and JSON Security Architecture
+
+## Overview
+
+Extensibility is central to 👍kanban: administrators can author custom fields, dynamic computed formulas, and WebAssembly (Wasm) logic to compute metadata in real time. However, allowing untrusted or semi-trusted script execution and arbitrary JSON payloads introduces critical attack vectors:
+1. **Supply-chain and Binary Tampering:** Substituting an approved Wasm module binary with a malicious payload after approval.
+2. **Re-entrant Elevation:** Calling privileged endpoints (such as `test-execute` or `dry-run`) from within custom field scripts or workflow hooks to bypass security boundaries.
+3. **Event-Loop CPU and Memory Denial-of-Service:** Exploiting Python abstract syntax tree (AST) evaluation through exponential operations, unbounded sequence allocations, or deep syntax tree exhaustion.
+4. **JSON Payload Bombs:** Crashing or freezing ASGI servers via nested JSON recursion (stack overflow), unbounded key allocation (memory exhaustion), or invalid UTF-16 lone surrogates.
+5. **Client-Side Prototype Pollution and DOM XSS:** Polluting JavaScript object prototypes via `__proto__` or `constructor` keys in parsed JSON, or injecting unvalidated HTML strings into the document object model.
+
+To eliminate these vulnerabilities, 👍kanban implements an end-to-end defense-in-depth architecture spanning ASGI middleware, database triggers, AST execution bounds, and browser sanitizers.
+
+---
+
+## Architectural Security Model
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    Client["Client / External Agent"] -->|HTTP / JSON Payload| JsonMiddleware["JsonLimitsMiddleware (ASGI)"]
+
+    subgraph Inbound Guardrails
+        JsonMiddleware -->|1. Size Check| SizeCheck{"Body <= 2 MiB / 25 MiB?"}
+        SizeCheck -- No --> R413["413 PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE"]
+        SizeCheck -- Yes --> SurrogateCheck{"UTF-16 Lone Surrogates?"}
+        SurrogateCheck -- Yes --> R422S["422 INVALID_UTF8_SURROGATE"]
+        SurrogateCheck -- No --> IterativeParser{"Iterative JSON Scanner"}
+        IterativeParser -->|Depth > 32| R422D["422 JSON_DEPTH_EXCEEDED"]
+        IterativeParser -->|Keys > 5000| R422K["422 JSON_KEYS_EXCEEDED"]
+        IterativeParser -->|Valid| Router["FastAPI Router"]
+    end
+
+    subgraph Endpoint & Re-entrancy Guards
+        Router --> ScriptGuard["ScriptDepthGuardMiddleware"]
+        ScriptGuard -->|X-Kanban-Script-Depth on Blocked Path| R409R["409 SCRIPT_RECURSION_BLOCKED"]
+        ScriptGuard --> AuthGate["PROJECT_ADMIN + AAL2 Gate"]
+        AuthGate -- Missing AAL2 --> R403AAL["403 AAL2_REQUIRED"]
+        AuthGate -- Unauthorized --> R403A["403 INSUFFICIENT_CAPABILITY"]
+        AuthGate -- Authorized --> ExecutionService["CustomFieldDefinitionService"]
+    end
+
+    subgraph Sandboxed Execution & Manifest Integrity
+        ExecutionService --> ManifestCheck{"Manifest SHA-256 Valid?"}
+        ManifestCheck -- Tampered --> TamperRevoke["PostgreSQL Tamper Trigger Revokes Escalation"]
+        ManifestCheck -- Valid --> ExecutorType{"Engine Type"}
+        ExecutorType -->|Wasm| WasmRegistry{"ApprovedWasmModule Verified?"}
+        WasmRegistry -- No --> R404W["404 WASM_MODULE_NOT_FOUND"]
+        WasmRegistry -- Yes --> WasmSandbox["Wasmtime Isolated Engine"]
+        ExecutorType -->|Safe Formula| ASTBounds["AST Bounds Checker"]
+        ASTBounds -->|Nodes > 64 or Depth > 8| RNone["Returns None (Status ERROR, Value null)"]
+        ASTBounds -->|Pow / Mult Bounds Check| ASTEval["_eval_safe_formula (Dict-Only Lookup)"]
+    end
+```
+
+---
+
+## 1. Wasm Module SHA-256 Binding and Manifest Integrity
+
+### Cryptographic Manifest Digest
+Custom field definitions can declare escalated permissions (such as workspace-level or server-level API read/write scopes) requiring cryptographic signatures and administrative approvals. Previously, only the script text was included in the manifest hash calculation.
+
+Under the hardened architecture (`kanban/custom_fields/manifest.py`), `compute_field_manifest_sha256` explicitly binds the compiled binary digest `wasm_module_sha256`. The canonical payload keys are:
+
+```python
+canonical_manifest = {
+    "credential_mode": credential_mode,
+    "egress_allowlist": sorted(egress_allowlist),
+    "output_format": output_format,
+    "output_format_metadata": output_format_metadata,
+    "script_source": script_source,
+    "target_scope": target_scope,
+    "tier": tier,
+    "wasm_module_sha256": wasm_module_sha256,
+}
+```
+
+### PostgreSQL Tamper-Revocation Trigger
+When an existing definition is updated, changing `wasm_module_sha256` marks `spec_changed = True` (`kanban/custom_fields/service.py`). The database trigger `custom_field_manifest_tamper_revoke` executes immediately:
+- Escalation approvals (`status IN ('PENDING', 'PENDING_SECOND_APPROVER', 'APPROVED')`) are automatically revoked (`status = 'REVOKED'`, `revoked_reason = 'MANIFEST_SHA256_CHANGED'`).
+- The manifest hash is regenerated against the new binary payload.
+- Any attempt to substitute an unapproved or modified WebAssembly binary invalidates existing approval records, preventing unauthorized privilege escalation.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Test-Execute Security and Re-entrancy Protection
+
+### Administrative Access Control
+The `POST /api/v1/projects/{project}/custom-fields/test-execute` endpoint allows testing custom field logic against draft ticket data before persisting to production. Because this endpoint executes script engines in real time, access is restricted:
+- **Requirement:** Callers must authenticate as `PROJECT_ADMIN` with Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (`AAL2`).
+- **Capability Check:** `CustomFieldDefinitionService.require_admin_and_aal2(session, caller, project)` verifies membership and enforces step-up authentication. Callers with AAL1 receive HTTP 403 `AAL2_REQUIRED`.
+- **Wasm Verification:** Wasm draft payloads are verified against the `ApprovedWasmModule` registry or approved hash store before execution. Unapproved Wasm modules return HTTP 404 `WASM_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`.
+
+### Re-entrancy and Recursion Blocking
+To prevent custom scripts or webhook handlers from calling administrative execution endpoints recursively, `ScriptDepthGuardMiddleware` (`kanban/api/middleware/script_depth.py`) intercepts outbound internal calls carrying `X-Kanban-Script-Depth`.
+
+The following paths are explicitly blocked from scripted invocations:
+- `/api/v1/projects/[^/]+/custom-fields/test-execute`
+- `/api/v1/projects/[^/]+/workflow-hooks/dry-run`
+
+Any scripted call attempting to reach these paths returns HTTP 409 `SCRIPT_RECURSION_BLOCKED`.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Formula AST Execution Bounds (Denial-of-Service Defense)
+
+Simple computed fields use Python AST formula evaluation (`kanban/custom_fields/executor.py`). While sandboxed, unconstrained AST operations could consume 100% of the asynchronous event loop CPU or allocate gigabytes of memory.
+
+The safe formula engine enforces static and dynamic limits:
+
+### Static AST Complexity Checks
+Before evaluation, `_check_formula_ast_bounds` traverses the AST tree:
+- **Node Count Limit:** The total number of AST nodes cannot exceed `64`.
+- **Depth Limit:** The maximum nesting depth of the AST tree cannot exceed `8`.
+- If either threshold is exceeded, `_check_formula_ast_bounds` / `_eval_safe_formula` returns `None` (and `test-execute` returns HTTP 200 with `status="ERROR", value=null`).
+
+### Arithmetic and Allocation Bounds
+- **Power Operator (`ast.Pow`):** Exponents are restricted to `<= 64`, and base values are restricted to `abs(base) <= 1_000_000`. Exponentiation errors like negative exponents on zero (`0 ** -1` or `0.0 ** -2`) catch `ZeroDivisionError` and return `None`. This prevents operations like `999999 ** 999999` or division errors from freezing or crashing the process.
+- **Multiplication Operator (`ast.Mult`):** Sequence multiplication (e.g. `'A' * 1000000` or `[0] * 1000000`) is bounded to a maximum output length of `4096` elements or characters.
+- **Attribute Access (`ast.Attribute`):** Attribute access on Python objects via `getattr` is eliminated. Only dictionary key lookups are permitted (`obj.get(attr)` or `obj[attr]` when `obj` is an instance of `dict`). Introspection attributes (`__class__`, `__mro__`, `__subclasses__`) cannot be resolved.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Global ASGI JSON Limits Middleware
+
+JSON parsing in Python web frameworks typically buffers the entire request into memory before deserializing. Malicious clients can crash workers using deeply nested arrays (`[[[[...]]]]`) or gigabyte payloads.
+
+`JsonLimitsMiddleware` (`kanban/api/middleware/json_limits.py`) sits at the ASGI level:
+
+### Streaming Body Size Caps
+- **Default Limit:** `2 MiB` (2,097,152 bytes) for standard JSON API requests.
+- **Extended Limit:** `25 MiB` (26,214,400 bytes) for designated attachment and import routes:
+  - `/attachments`
+  - `/imports`
+  - `/api/v1/attachments`
+  - `/api/v1/admin/imports`
+- Bodies exceeding the limit are rejected immediately with HTTP 413 `PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE` before reaching the application framework.
+
+### UTF-16 Lone-Surrogate Rejection
+Python strings and JSON encoders can be vulnerable to unpaired surrogate code points (`0xD800` through `0xDFFF`), which cause database serialization errors or security bypasses.
+- The middleware scans raw incoming bytes for invalid surrogate sequences before passing data to FastAPI.
+- Requests containing lone surrogates receive HTTP 422 `Unprocessable Entity` with error code `INVALID_UTF8_SURROGATE`.
+
+### Non-Recursive Iterative Structural Validation
+To protect against stack overflows without paying the performance cost of complete parsing twice, the middleware uses an iterative character scanner for `application/json` and `+json` content types:
+- **Maximum Depth:** `MAX_JSON_DEPTH = 32`. Nested objects or arrays deeper than 32 levels return HTTP 422 `JSON_DEPTH_EXCEEDED`.
+- **Maximum Keys:** `MAX_JSON_KEYS = 5000`. Payloads containing more than 5,000 keys return HTTP 422 `JSON_KEYS_EXCEEDED`.
+- **Passthrough:** Multipart form data, Server-Sent Events (SSE), and static asset requests bypass JSON scanning entirely.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Client-Side Safe JSON and Trusted Types
+
+Security invariants extend directly to the browser client (`kanban/web/`):
+
+### Safe JSON Parsing (`safeJsonParse`)
+Standard `JSON.parse` is vulnerable to Prototype Pollution when handling untrusted JSON payloads containing `__proto__`, `constructor`, or `prototype` keys.
+
+The utility `safeJsonParse` (`kanban/web/src/utils/safeJson.ts`) applies an iterative reviver function that removes these keys from the resulting object:
+- In `draftsStore.ts`, all draft restoration routines use `safeJsonParse`.
+- In `CustomFieldDefinitionEditor.tsx`, format metadata and formula test inputs are deserialized using `safeJsonParse`.
+
+```typescript
+export function safeJsonParse<T = unknown>(text: string): T {
+  return JSON.parse(text, (key, value) => {
+    if (key === '__proto__' || key === 'constructor' || key === 'prototype') {
+      return undefined;
+    }
+    return value;
+  });
+}
+```
+
+### Unified Trusted Types Policy
+In `kanban/web/src/editor/clipboard/trustedTypes.ts`, the `kanban-sanitizer` and `dompurify` Trusted Types policies ensure that any HTML passed to browser sinks is sanitized through `DOMPurify.sanitize(html, { RETURN_TRUSTED_TYPE: false })` before being wrapped as a `TrustedHTML` token.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Verification and Audit Matrix
+
+| Security Layer | Implementation File | Verification Test | Expected Defense Behavior |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| **Wasm Hash Binding** | `kanban/custom_fields/manifest.py` | `test_manifest_and_formula_security.py` | Modifying `wasm_module_sha256` alters `manifest_sha256` and revokes approval via `custom_field_manifest_tamper_revoke`. |
+| **Admin test-execute Gate** | `kanban/api/v1/custom_field_execution.py` | `test_manifest_and_formula_security.py` | Non-admin returns 403 `INSUFFICIENT_CAPABILITY`; AAL1 returns 403 `AAL2_REQUIRED`; unapproved Wasm returns 404 `WASM_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. |
+| **Script Depth Guard** | `kanban/api/middleware/script_depth.py` | `test_script_depth_middleware.py` | Re-entrant `test-execute` or `dry-run` returns 409 `SCRIPT_RECURSION_BLOCKED`. |
+| **AST Node & Depth Bounds** | `kanban/custom_fields/executor.py` | `test_manifest_and_formula_security.py` | Nodes > 64 or depth > 8 returns `None` (test-execute returns 200 `status="ERROR", value=null`). |
+| **AST Math & Sequence Bounds**| `kanban/custom_fields/executor.py` | `test_safe_formula_unit.py` | `ast.Pow` bounded to 64; `0 ** -1` returns `None`; sequence mult bounded to 4096; dict-only attrs. |
+| **ASGI Size Caps** | `kanban/api/middleware/json_limits.py` | `test_json_limits_middleware.py` | Payloads > 2 MiB (or > 25 MiB attachments/imports) return HTTP 413 `PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE`. |
+| **ASGI Surrogate Rejection**| `kanban/api/middleware/json_limits.py` | `test_json_limits_middleware.py` | Lone surrogates `0xD800..0xDFFF` return HTTP 422 `INVALID_UTF8_SURROGATE`. |
+| **ASGI JSON Depth / Keys** | `kanban/api/middleware/json_limits.py` | `test_json_limits_middleware.py` | Depth > 32 returns 422 `JSON_DEPTH_EXCEEDED`; keys > 5000 returns 422 `JSON_KEYS_EXCEEDED`. |
+| **Client Safe JSON** | `kanban/web/src/utils/safeJson.ts` | `safeJson.test.ts` | Strips `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` preventing prototype pollution. |
+| **Client Trusted Types** | `kanban/web/src/editor/clipboard/trustedTypes.ts` | `trustedTypes.test.ts` | Mandatory `DOMPurify.sanitize` execution on all `createHTML` calls. |
